# 2. Example Problem

Suppose the user selects:

```text
Sheet: Summary
Cell: F2
```

and F2 contains:

```excel
=IFERROR(
    VLOOKUP(A2,Customer_Master!A:D,4,FALSE)
    *
    INDEX(Rates!B:D,MATCH(B2,Rates!B:B,0),3)
    +
    SUMIFS(
        Commission!D:D,
        Commission!A:A,A2,
        Commission!B:B,"Loan"
    ),
0)
```

The application must NOT simply display:

```text
F2 = 57,500
```

Instead it must explain:

```text
F2
│
├── IFERROR
│
├── VLOOKUP
│   ├── Lookup value: A2
│   │   └── CUST1001
│   │
│   ├── Lookup range: Customer_Master!A:D
│   │
│   ├── Match type: FALSE / Exact
│   │
│   ├── Matched row: Customer_Master!15
│   │
│   └── Returned value: D15 = 50,000
│
├── INDEX / MATCH
│   ├── MATCH lookup value: B2
│   │   └── India
│   │
│   ├── MATCH result: Row 8
│   │
│   ├── INDEX source: Rates!B:D
│   │
│   └── Returned value: 1.10
│
├── Multiplication
│   └── 50,000 × 1.10
│       └── 55,000
│
├── SUMIFS
│   ├── ID = CUST1001
│   ├── Type = Loan
│   ├── Matching rows = 12, 27
│   ├── Row 12 = 1,500
│   ├── Row 27 = 1,000
│   └── Result = 2,500
│
└── Final calculation
    └── 55,000 + 2,500
        = 57,500
```

This level of explanation is the core requirement.

