# 5. Formula Parser

Build a proper formula parser rather than relying only on string manipulation.

The parser must convert formulas into an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).

For example:

```excel
=A1*(B1+C1)
```

must become conceptually:

```text
MULTIPLY
│
├── A1
│
└── ADD
    ├── B1
    └── C1
```

For:

```excel
=IF(A1>100,B1*C1,D1)
```

produce:

```text
IF
│
├── CONDITION
│   └── A1 > 100
│
├── TRUE_BRANCH
│   └── B1 * C1
│
└── FALSE_BRANCH
    └── D1
```

The AST is critical because the application must understand the logical structure of the formula.

