# 8. Recursive Backtracking

This is the most important feature.

If:

```text
F2 → VLOOKUP → D15
```

and D15 itself contains:

```excel
=C15*E15
```

the analyzer MUST continue tracing.

Therefore:

```text
F2
 ↓
VLOOKUP
 ↓
Customer_Master!D15
 ↓
C15 × E15
 ↓
C15
 ↓
E15
```

The engine must recursively traverse the dependency graph until it reaches:

* hardcoded values
* external workbook references
* unsupported formulas
* intentionally ignored cells
* circular references

Do not stop at the first formula cell.

